---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { hospital } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Hospital Information"
  subtitle="Registered details, accreditation, services and statutory information."
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>About {hospital.name}</h2>
  <p>
    {hospital.name} is a multi-specialty hospital located in {hospital.address.city}, {hospital.address.state}, serving
    patients from {hospital.address.city} and the surrounding districts since {hospital.foundedYear}. We provide
    out-patient, in-patient, critical-care, maternity and diagnostic services.
  </p>

  <h2>Registered Address</h2>
  <p>
    {hospital.name}<br />
    {hospital.address.line1}, {hospital.address.line2}<br />
    {hospital.address.city}, {hospital.address.state} — {hospital.address.pincode}<br />
    India
  </p>

  <h2>Accreditation &amp; Quality</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>NABH Certified</strong> — accredited by the National Accreditation Board for Hospitals &amp; Healthcare Providers.</li>
    <li>Quality systems aligned to NABH standards, including patient-safety, infection-control and quality-improvement programmes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Out-patient consultation across multiple specialties.</li>
    <li>24 × 7 Emergency and Intensive Care (ICU).</li>
    <li>In-patient wards and maternity services.</li>
    <li>Diagnostics — laboratory and imaging, as available.</li>
    <li>Ambulance services and community health camps.</li>
    <li>Teleconsultation for suitable, non-emergency conditions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Timings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>OPD:</strong> {hospital.hours.opd} (Monday to Saturday).</li>
    <li><strong>Emergency &amp; ICU:</strong> 24 × 7, including Sundays and public holidays.</li>
    <li><strong>Pharmacy:</strong> 24 × 7.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Emergency Contact</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hospital emergency line (24 × 7):</strong> {hospital.phones.emergency}</li>
    <li><strong>Ambulance:</strong> {hospital.phones.ambulance} (hospital) · 108 (national free ambulance)</li>
    <li><strong>All-in-one national emergency:</strong> 112</li>
    <li><strong>Women helpline:</strong> 181</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Key Policies &amp; Patient Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/patient-rights">Patient Rights &amp; Responsibilities</a></li>
    <li><a href="/patient-guide">Patient &amp; Visitor Guide</a></li>
    <li><a href="/grievance">Grievance Redressal</a></li>
    <li><a href="/refund-cancellation">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="/insurance">Insurance &amp; TPA</a></li>
    <li><a href="/telemedicine">Telemedicine &amp; Teleconsultation</a></li>
    <li><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> · <a href="/disclaimer">Medical Disclaimer</a></li>
    <li><a href="/accessibility">Accessibility Statement</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Statutory and Regulatory Information</h2>
  <p>
    The hospital operates in accordance with applicable Indian law, including the Clinical Establishments Act, 2010, where
    applicable, the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, biomedical-waste management rules, and the registration and licensing
    requirements of the State of {hospital.address.state}. Clinical establishments and pharmacies operate under the
    requisite licences issued by the competent authorities.
  </p>
  <p>
    Registered medical practitioners practising at the hospital hold valid registration with the relevant State Medical
    Council or the National Medical Commission. Doctor registration numbers are available on request and, where displayed,
    on individual doctor profiles.
  </p>

  <h2>Medical Records</h2>
  <p>
    Medical records are maintained and retained in accordance with applicable law and professional regulations. Patients, or
    their authorised representatives, may request copies of records by contacting the hospital. Requests are processed after
    verifying identity, and statutory retention periods apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Anti-Fraud and Grievance</h2>
  <p>
    Concerns regarding billing, treatment, safety or conduct may be raised through our
    <a href="/grievance">Grievance Redressal</a> process. Reports of suspected fraud or impersonation may be directed to
    the hospital administration.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {hospital.name}<br />
    {hospital.address.line1}, {hospital.address.line2}, {hospital.address.city}, {hospital.address.state} — {hospital.address.pincode}<br />
    Reception: {hospital.phones.reception} · Appointments: {hospital.phones.appointment}<br />
    Email: {hospital.email}
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
